1
00:00:00,400 --> 00:00:03,047
This pale line through Alabama isn't a
road.

2
00:00:03,347 --> 00:00:07,355
It wasn't there before April
twenty-seventh, twenty-eleven.

3
00:00:07,655 --> 00:00:09,929
It's a tornado damage scar.

4
00:00:10,230 --> 00:00:13,451
NASA photographed it from orbit five days
later.

5
00:00:13,750 --> 00:00:18,726
The storm left a trail through Tuscaloosa,
and other satellites caught more scars

6
00:00:18,726 --> 00:00:19,832
across the region.

7
00:00:20,132 --> 00:00:24,233
This is what a tornado can leave behind,
visible from space.
